**.idea/
**.claude/

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
**target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
**Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk


# Added by cargo

/target
Cargo.lock

# Python bytecode from the ci/ helper scripts.
__pycache__/

# Local design docs / plans / investigation reports (never committed; the
# issue tracker covers real defects and measurable optimisations, docs/ is
# for everything else — same convention as the sibling smear repo).
#
# Root-anchored on purpose: a leading "/" with no "**" prefix. A bare
# `docs/` or a `**`-prefixed `**docs/` both match a docs/ directory at
# *any* depth (git only anchors a pattern via a leading or middle slash;
# a trailing slash alone does not anchor it), which would also catch a
# nested `*/docs/` some crate might add later. `/docs/` matches only the
# top-level tree, which is the actual intent. (Mirrors `/target` above,
# which is already anchored the same way.)
/docs/
